---
source: tests/cli_capture.rs
expression: r.stdout
---
capture: new profile `mine`
into:    <HOME>/.local/share/ricepilot/profiles/mine

<HOME>/.config/hypr  ->  <profile>/hypr
  2 director(ies), 3 file(s), 2 symlink(s), 52 byte(s)

  1 absolute symlink(s) inside the tree. ricepilot copies a link as a link and
  never rewrites one, so each of these keeps pointing where it points now:
    userChrome.css -> <HOME>/.config/hypr/scripts/configs.fish  (back into this tree)

  1 file(s) only their owner can read. a mode-600 file in a config tree is
  usually a token or a key; consider declaring it `volatile` so its content is
  not hashed into a manifest:
    0600  secret.token

profile.toml as it will be written:
  # written by `ricepilot capture mine`.
  # it is yours to edit. ricepilot only rewrites it to append a [[path]] when you
  # `ricepilot adopt` something into this profile.
  name = "mine"
  volatile = []
  generated = []
  
  [[path]]
  dest       = "~/.config/hypr"
  src        = "hypr"
  kind       = "dir-link"
  activation = "relogin"

nothing has been changed. re-run with --commit to capture.
capture copies into a profile; it does not activate anything and does not touch any
live path.
